I walk into a large clothing store.
I look at the new spring clothes.
There are many light jackets and shirts hanging.
I look slowly around the store.
Everything looks fresh and spring-like.
Suddenly I see a very nice jacket.
It is light green.
I take it down from the hanger.
I would like to try it on.
There is a large mirror standing on the floor.
So I do not need a fitting room.
I put the light green jacket on.
I look at myself in the mirror.
The jacket fits really well.
It is not too big and not too small.
It actually fits perfectly.
The color is also pretty on me.
I smile at the mirror.
I take the jacket off again.
I decide to buy it.
